 "observations": [
  "col_left L1: «Ts‘ai C‘in» is printed with the turned commas ‘ after the s and the C.",
  "col_left L2: «*unbūb muǵawwaf*» is printed in italics, with the bar over the second u and the acute on the g. The second a of «muǵawwaf» is printed broken: of its bowl only a speck at mid height and a piece at its foot printed, beside its stem (like ·x), read at 8,000 dpi; read a. A speck (0.6 by 0.4 point) after the point of «lin.» is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L5: «aṭ-Ṭūsī» has the dots under the t and the T and the bars over the u and the i; its hyphen is printed short (2.2 by 1.3 points), with a speck (0.7 point) under its right end. «Naṣīr ad-dīn» has the dot under the s and the bars over the i's.",
  "col_left L5, L6, col_right L3, L4: a space of two blank lines (42.2–42.7 points from baseline to baseline) separates the names in T from those in U (left column) and the names in U from those in V (right column).",
  "col_left L6: «*‘ūbā*» is printed in italics, with the bars over the u and the a. Under its sign of ‘ayn (1.8 by 3.8 points, 3.4–7.2 points above the baseline) stands a round point (1.3 by 1.2 points, 0.8–2.0 points above the baseline), so that the two look like ‘ set over a point, read at 8,000 dpi; the signs of ‘ayn in L13, L34 and L36 have none. The point is not transcribed. The Syriac «ܥܘܒ݁ܐ» (‘ubbā, the bosom) is printed in Serto, read at 10,000 dpi: ‘e, waw, beth with a dot above it (qushshaya, transcribed with U+0741) and the final alaph.",
  "col_left L7: «*uccastha*» is printed in italics.",
  "col_left L10, L11: «*Prolegomena*» and «*catalogus fixarum*» are printed in italics.",
  "col_left L13: «‘Umar» begins with the sign of ‘ayn; «Muḥ.» has the dot under the h; «al-Kindī» has the bar over the last i.",
  "col_left L15: a speck (0.7 by 0.6 point) after «eius», on the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L16: the opening parenthesis of «(tangentium» is printed broken, like {; read (.",
  "col_left L17: a blot joined below the end of the last a of «theoremata» (1.2 by 1.9 points, 0.9–2.8 points above the baseline), like a tail of the a, is not transcribed; it stands above the baseline and is not a point.",
  "col_left L25: the m of «umbra» is printed broken, like ın; read m.",
  "col_left L27, L30, L31: «al-Battānī» and «Battānī» have the bars over the second a and the last i.",
  "col_left L28: the o of «ratione» is printed broken, its right side missing; read o.",
  "col_left L33: «*ūpīqurūs*» is printed in italics, with the bars over the first u, the i and the second u. The Syriac «ܐܘܦܝܩܪܘܣ» (Epicurus) is printed in Serto, read at 9,000 dpi: alaph, waw, pe, yod, qoph, rish (with its dot above), waw, semkath; no waw stands between the qoph and the rish (pe, yod, qoph and rish are joined in one stroke).",
  "col_left L34, L36: «*‘urf al-asad*» and «*‘urqūb ar-rāmī*» are printed in italics, with the sign of ‘ayn and the bars over the u, the a and the i; «β» is Greek.",
  "col_left L37: «ω» is Greek.",
  "col_left L37: a round speck (1.1 by 1.0 points, 1.6–2.6 points above the baseline) between the u and the m of «appositum» is not transcribed; it stands above the baseline and is not a point.",
  "col_left L38: between «281» and «ad» a small comma (1.1 by 1.7 points, its foot on the baseline) stands 3.7 points after the 1 and 1.6 points before the a, read at 8,000 dpi; transcribed as printed, «281 ,ad». A thin raised stroke (0.8 by 1.6 points, 5.2–6.8 points above the baseline) after «ad» is not transcribed. «16{sup:am}» is printed with the raised small «am».",
  "col_left L3, L36, col_right L21: the upper and the lower ball of the 3 of «34», of «*183*» and of «253» stand apart from the figure, like a colon before it; read 34, 183, 253.",
