  "col_left, col_right: the ball terminals of the 3s often stand apart from the figure (69 loose pieces listed by loose_pieces.py, with the real points); low on the line like points stand the lower balls of the 3s of «313» (L7), «3» (L8, R7, R10 twice, R20), «347» (L12), «325» (L13), «*23*» (L19), «39-41» (L23), «*183*» (L36), «252-253» (R21), «230» (R29), «273» (R30) and «278-283» (R33), the tail of the 9 of «249» (R40) and the ends of the feet of the small capitals «{sc:lxxv}» (L3) and «{sc:l}» (L9). None of them is a point.",
  "notes_left L1: the rule over the footnote (115.1 points long, from 225.8 to 340.9, at 729.15, across the column rule) is printed slightly tilted, its left end 0.9 point lower than its right; it lies 22.0 points below the last lines of the columns. The footnote belongs to «(1)» in L40 of the right column and runs on to the next page.",
